# Raises since the last measured reduction, per registered path (V123).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `.context-limits` sets a ceiling, and a ceiling's
# remedy when it fires is a raise -- one line, versus a day of compaction.
# So the cheap move wins every time, and it has: SPEC.md's ceiling has been
# raised ten times and the file compacted twice. The eighth, ninth and
# tenth raises each wrote "the next one should be refused until a
# compaction runs" into that file's prose, and nothing read it.
#
# This is that sentence, as data. The guard in `tests/spec_compact.rs`
# refuses an increment past the number below, so the next raise fails until
# a reduction resets the count to 0.
#
# WHAT COUNTS AS A REDUCTION: the file's own token count FELL against the
# base. Not a promise, not an intention -- a measurement, of the same kind
# `itok check` already makes. T107 did it to README: 5,753 -> 5,110 tokens,
# and 6,500 -> 5,800 on the ceiling, which is the first reduction this
# repo records.
#
# THE NUMBER ONLY EVER COMES DOWN, like `.coverage` and the ceilings
# themselves. Raising the cap here is not a fix; it is the thing this file
# exists to stop being done quietly.
#
# WHY NOT A THIRD COLUMN in `.context-limits`: that parser SKIPS a row it
# cannot read (B7), silently, so a widened shape would risk disabling the
# ceiling to save a file. A separate registry costs one more read and
# cannot break the gate it stands beside.

